Fix GDMS 404 - v0.120 "fixed" a URL segment that wasn't broken (v0.121)

v0.120 got login working, but the channel calls started 404ing instead
of the earlier auth error - a sign the URL itself still didn't exist.

Re-checking the doc more carefully: every sample request/example URL
for these endpoints only ever shows the unresolved "{version}"
placeholder, never a literal value. v0.120 filled it in from each
endpoint's own apiDoc metadata field, "version": "1.0.0" - but that
field is apiDoc's own internal doc-spec version tag (every entry in
the whole file has one, unrelated to URLs), not the literal segment.

The actual substitution rule is spelled out in plain English on the
"Get Start" page, which v0.120 didn't re-check once it thought the
sample-request fields had the answer: "{version} is version number:
The value is 'v' + current version number, such as v1.0.0, v1.1.0."
So the segment is "v1.0.0" - exactly what the very first
implementation used, before v0.120 "corrected" it to "1.0.0" and
broke it.

Reverted GdmsAuthService#baseUrl() back to "/oapi/v1.0.0". The other
two v0.120 fixes - authBaseUrl() being unversioned for the token
endpoints, and GdmsChannelService prefixing every path with
"/channel" - were correct per the doc's sampleRequest fields and are
unchanged.

gdms-api-findings.md (project doc) updated with this correction and a
lesson-learned note: when a doc's examples only show an unresolved
placeholder, resolve it from the prose page that documents the
substitution rule, not from a same-named metadata field that happens
to have a plausible value.

